# tools/bootstrap.ref: the chain of pinned commits that builds the compiler.
#
# One line per pin, oldest first, `bootstrap-<n> <40-hex sha>`. The sha is the
# fact and the tag of the same name is a name for it. stage1, the C bootstrap,
# builds pin 0's src/fort with pin 0's std; pin k builds pin k+1's tree with
# its own std; the last pin builds HEAD's src/fort with HEAD's std into
# build/<preset>/stage2/fort. Every pin is a commit of this repository, so a
# shallow clone cannot build (notes/compiler.md 8, invariant 4).
#
# A pin moves only on need, and the need is one of two things: HEAD's src/fort
# or std wants a form the last pin cannot compile, or HEAD's tree lacks a file
# the last pin's compiler demands by name. The move is its own commit -- this
# line and a note naming the need -- so the gate proves the new chain before
# HEAD relies on it. tools/pin.sh verify reads this file at configure time.
#
# bootstrap-1 moves for the second reason (T-132). Pin 0's loader reads
# <std-dir>/rt_float.ft into any closure that holds a float, and T-132 folded
# the float printers into std/rt.ft, which stands in every closure. So pin 0
# demands std/rt_float.ft of HEAD, and HEAD cannot delete it: the build ends
# with `std/rt_float.ft:1:1: error: cannot read`. Pin 1 is the commit of the
# fold, whose src/fort names rt_float nowhere, so it asks for no such file and
# HEAD deletes it in the commit after this one.
bootstrap-0 d132989636052c4a8a01887aa86103cd64c4f2a7
bootstrap-1 7944120ff6e5701bcf0888a0c95a7e7616dc9578
